From 10d664a08d5f886c000025d718132639af8ae712 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:01:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] Recover the RBBR phase machine and RTT sampling logic

Reconstruct the remaining tcp_rbbr.c bodies from the 13432 reference.

- Decode the complete rbbr_update_phase state machine: the PROBE_RTT
  round analysis (median, plateau detection, jitter reset, conclude
  decision), the PROBE_RWND per-cycle growth/hold/exit paths, and the
  CRUISE sawtooth and backoff action accounting.
- Add the RTT sample ring buffer, median-of-deviations jitter
  estimator, sawtooth queue-competition detection and PROBE_RTT
  entry.
- Implement tcp_rbbr_data_rcvd, including the win-converged gating of
  samples and the two per-site rate-limited net_uptime() logs.
- Rebuild enter_probe_rwnd, enter_cruise and apply_cruise_backoff on
  the rbbr_update_win/rbbr_pct/rbbr_min_win helpers, matching the
  reference call structure.
- Measure the rbbr_action_elapsed duration branch from
  cycle_measure_ts as the reference does.
- Give the tcp_utils.c helpers external linkage and pull in tcp_seq.h
  for the sequence comparison macros.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
